cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research, please cite it as below."
title: "Reverse-Engineering Analysis: Installing Signed OTA Updates on TCL Google TVs (G10/55C655) Without Removable Media"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A reproducible reverse-engineering study of the firmware-update paths of a
  TCL Google TV (Realtek RTD platform, Android TV 12). The study documents why
  a vendor-signed update package cannot be installed without a USB block
  medium, the vendor OTA server, or the vendor signing key, and evidences each
  blocked path with code-level findings and live tests. All device identifiers
  are redacted for data-protection compliance.
keywords:
  - firmware update
  - OTA
  - Android TV
  - reverse engineering
  - A/B updates
  - recovery
  - digital signature
  - device security
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/StevenDawrell/tcl-update-research"
authors:
  - name: "TCL Update Research Contributors"
    alias: "StevenDawrell"
